        `<b>Register:</b> Move between registers deliberately. A contract or budget uses formal, precise language; a promotional caption can be lively and colloquial; a performance review uses the technical vocabulary of dance, drama, music or film. Using the wrong register costs credibility.`,
        `<b>Audience profiling:</b> In the arts, "audience" means two things: the people who watch the show and the people who fund it. Profile both. A sponsor wants brand visibility and community impact; a cultural festival audience wants authenticity and entertainment.`,
        `<b>Source evaluation:</b> Reviews, social media buzz and ticket-sales claims are not neutral. Ask who wrote the review, whether a promoter posted the figures, and whether attendance data comes from the box office or an estimate before using it as evidence.`
